## 24\. Essential engineering equations and quantities to recognize

These are not just vocabulary terms. They are relationships you will repeatedly use throughout mechanical engineering.

| Concept | Relationship | Typical use |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Newton's second law | $F=ma$ | Motion and force analysis |
| Moment of a force | $M=Fd_\perp$ | Rotation and equilibrium |
| Translational power | $P=Fv$ | Linear motion |
| Rotational power | $P=T\omega$ | Motors, shafts, turbines |
| Normal stress | $\sigma=F/A$ | Axial loading |
| Normal strain | $\epsilon=\Delta L/L_0$ | Deformation |
| Hooke's law | $\sigma=E\epsilon$ | Linear elastic behavior |
| Axial elongation | $\Delta L=FL/(AE)$ | Uniform prismatic bar, linear elasticity |
| Density | $\rho=m/V$ | Materials and fluids |
| Pressure | $p=F/A$ | Fluids and contact loading |
| Hydrostatic pressure change | $\Delta p=\rho g\Delta h$ | Liquid columns |
| Flow continuity | $\dot m=\rho AV$ | Flow calculations |
| Reynolds number | $Re=\rho VD/\mu$ | Flow-regime assessment in pipes |
| Ideal gas law | $PV=mRT$ | Gas thermodynamics |
| First-law energy balance | $\Delta E=Q-W$ | Closed-system energy analysis |
| Fourier's law | $\dot Q=-kA\,dT/dx$ | Conduction |
| Newton's cooling law | $\dot Q=hA(T_s-T_\infty)$ | Convection |
| Thermal resistance | $R_{\rm th}=\Delta T/\dot Q$ | Heat-transfer networks |
| Spring force | $F=kx$ | Linear spring behavior |
| Rotational inertia | $T=I\alpha$ | Rotational dynamics |
| Gear speed ratio | $n_1/n_2=Z_2/Z_1$ | Simple external gear pairs |
| Electrical power, DC | $P=VI$ | Electrical systems |
| Motor efficiency | $\eta=P_{\rm out}/P_{\rm in}$ | Energy conversion |
| Factor of safety | $FoS=\text{capacity}/\text{demand}$ | Design assessment |

_Symbols and sign conventions vary by discipline. In particular, the first-law expression above uses__$Q$__positive into the system and__$W$__positive out of the system._

